{"sounds":{"intro":"This is Khalkha Mongolian, the standard language of Mongolia, written in Cyrillic. Vowels follow harmony: back vowels (а, о, у, ы) and front vowels (э, ө, ү, и) do not mix in one word.","rows":[["ө","like \"ur\" in \"fur\", rounded lips","өдөр (UH-dur)"],["ү","like German \"ü\"","үг (ug)"],["х","kh, like Scottish \"loch\"","хоол (khool)"],["г","g (at the end of a word it is soft, like a voiced \"kh\")","гэр (ger)"],["ж","j, like \"judge\"","жаргал (jar-GAL)"],["з","dz, like \"adze\"","зуун (dzoon)"],["ц","ts, like \"cats\"","цай (tsai)"],["ч","ch, like \"church\"","чи (chee)"],["ш","sh","шөнө (SHU-nu)"],["ы","like \"ee\" in \"see\" said further back","ы (ee)"],["ъ / ь","a sign with no sound: it only shows hard or soft","хэлэх (KHE-lekh)"]],"notes":["Long vowels are written double: аа, ээ, оо, өө, уу, үү. Stress falls on the first syllable, unless the next syllable has a long vowel.","Mongolian has no gender and no articles. The verb comes last. Mongolian is written in Cyrillic, so there is no separate transliteration."]},"numbers":[{"id":"0-to-10","title":"0 to 10","items":[["zero","тэг","teg"],["one","нэг","neg"],["two","хоёр","KHO-yor"],["three","гурав","GOO-rav"],["four","дөрөв","DUR-uv"],["five","тав","tav"],["six","зургаа","DZOOR-gaa"],["seven","долоо","DOL-oo"],["eight","найм","naim"],["nine","ес","yes"],["ten","арав","A-rav"]]},{"id":"11-to-20","title":"11 to 20","items":[["eleven","арван нэг","A-rvan neg"],["twelve","арван хоёр","A-rvan KHO-yor"],["thirteen","арван гурав","A-rvan GOO-rav"],["fourteen","арван дөрөв","A-rvan DUR-uv"],["fifteen","арван тав","A-rvan tav"],["sixteen","арван зургаа","A-rvan DZOOR-gaa"],["seventeen","арван долоо","A-rvan DOL-oo"],["eighteen","арван найм","A-rvan naim"],["nineteen","арван ес","A-rvan yes"],["twenty","хорь","khor"]]},{"id":"tens-and-big-numbers","title":"Tens and big numbers","items":[["twenty-one","хорин нэг","KHO-rin neg"],["thirty","гуч","gooch"],["thirty-one","гучин нэг","GOO-chin neg"],["fort